Appendix AV

Framework Clarification:

SCARLET 2.0 utilizes Big Bang Nucleosynthesis (BBN) light-element abundance data ($Y_p$, $D/H$, ${}^7\text{Li}$) exclusively as a low-energy observational boundary condition, while explicitly rejecting the standard Hot Big Bang expansion paradigm.

In SCARLET 2.0, there is no initial singularity, no standard FLRW metric expansion, and no hot fluid cooling through a standard thermodynamic freeze-out. Instead, what standard cosmology interprets as the "BBN epoch" is purely the local metric-affine crystallization transition at $t_c = 3.5064\text{ s}$ ($x_\tau = 95.66057$), where spatial geometry flows from $d_s \approx 2 \to 4$. Elemental ratios—including the suppression of Lithium-7—are governed by the discrete quasicrystalline topology and metric-affine contortion dynamics of the substrate, rather than an expanding thermal radiation bath.

